* Modded-British 100 W three-mode head, preamp ("BE-100 v2", schematic rev 1.5, drawn by Patrice Frey, layout by Equinox).
* Input, V1A, then three modes chosen by two relays: Clean (V1A taps into a passive Bass / Treble stack and V1B, then straight to
* the power amp), BE (the guitar straight into V2A) and HBE (V1A into V2A, the hotter one). The BE / HBE chain is V2A, a switched
* voicing network (S2) with the FAT cap (SW9), V2B, the GAIN pot, V3A, V3B (a cathode follower) with the SAT clipper (SW7) and
* the VOICE switch (SW3), a Marshall-type stack (Treble, Middle, Bass) and the Master.
*
* Not modelled: the FX loop (the two depletion MOSFET buffers; the loop is wired through), the Line Out, the second pole of RELAY1
* and its ground contact, the heater wiring and the +12 V relay supply.
*
* Reading notes where the drawing is hard to follow (change them here, not in code):
*  - RELAY1 chooses what V2A hears: the raw input (BE) or V1A's output (HBE). RELAY2 chooses the output: the clean chain (Clean)
*    or the Master (BE and HBE). Which relay a mode energises is not printed; this is the reading that makes the modes make sense.
*  - the SAT clipper is 10k + 100n from V3B's cathode into two back-to-back MPSA06 junctions to ground (here two diodes), with 1M.
*  - the clean chain's tap is the junction of R9 and R3 on V1A's plate (the drawing runs a long wire from it to R25 / C10).
*  - the netlist is written in the Clean state (the first mode).

* Rail node x (after the 10k + 4.7k from B+), driven from the power amp at run time; R34 10k then 10k + 100u for V3.
V VRAIL x 100 430
R R34 x x2 10k
C C28 x 0 22u
C C29 x2 0 22u
R R43 x2 x3 10k
C C30 x3 0 100u
* The guitar behind a variable source resistance.
I VIN gin 1
R RSRC gin in 7k
* The guitar behind its source impedance. RSRC is the plain 7k source: the "Off" setting, and what a pedal in front of the amp
* looks like. A pickup replaces it with its own impedance as seen from the open-circuit voltage (the recording): the
* coil (winding resistance RPU + inductance) in parallel with its winding capacitance CPU and an eddy-current loss resistor
* RPL, then the cable capacitance (200 pF per 2 m, switched in steps of 200, 400 and 800 pF). The engine sets the values:
* single coil = coil 1 (2.5 H), humbucker and P-90 = coil 2 (5 H) with their own resistances; open = 1e12.
R RPU1 gin pkb1 1e12
.xfmr LPU1 L=2.5
  W pkb1 in 1 pu
.end
R RPU2 gin pkb2 1e12
.xfmr LPU2 L=5
  W pkb2 in 1 pu
.end
C CPU gin in 110p
R RPL gin in 1e12
R SWK1 in pkk1 1e12
C CCAB1 pkk1 0 200p
R SWK2 in pkk2 1e12
C CCAB2 pkk2 0 400p
R SWK4 in pkk4 1e12
C CCAB4 pkk4 0 800p


* Input jack: 1M to ground, 33k stopper into V1A (2.7k / 0.68u cathode, 220k + 100k plate load, 500p across the 100k).
R RJ1 in 0 1M
R R2 in ng1 33k
T V1A ng1 p1 k1 12AX7
R R9 x n1 220k
R R3 n1 p1 100k
C C8 n1 p1 500p
R R4 k1 0 2k7
C C5 k1 0 0.68u

* RELAY1: what V2A hears. V1A's output goes through 2.2n and 1M with 68k to ground; or the raw input.
C C3 p1 c3n 2n2
R R5 c3n v1o 1M
R R6 v1o 0 68k
R SW_RAW in v2s 1
R SW_V1 v1o v2s 1e12
R R11 v2s 0 10M
R R7 v2s ng2 33k

* V2A (2.7k / 0.68u cathode, 220k + 100k plate load with 500p) into the voicing network.
T V2A ng2 p2 k2 12AX7
R R18 x n2 220k
R R17 n2 p2 100k
C C13 n2 p2 500p
R R10 k2 0 2k7
C C20 k2 0 0.68u
C C14 p2 f2 2n2
C C15 p2 fat 22n
R SW_FAT fat f2 1e12
* S2 (two poles): position 1 puts 560k with 680p across it in series and 220k to ground; position 2 puts 68k in series and
* 68k to ground. R23 33k into V2B's grid.
R R20 f2 s2a 560k
C C16 f2 s2a 680p
R SW_S2A s2a g2c 1
R R19 f2 s2b 68k
R SW_S2B s2b g2c 1e12
R R26 g2c r26 220k
R SW_S2C r26 0 1
R R16 g2c r16 68k
R SW_S2D r16 0 1e12
R R23 g2c ng3 33k

* V2B (2.7k / 0.68u cathode, 100k plate load), 2.2n into the GAIN pot (1M), 470k || 500p into V3A's grid (470k to ground).
T V2B ng3 p3 kb 12AX7
R R21 x p3 100k
R R24 kb 0 2k7
C C17 kb 0 0.68u
C C19 p3 gt 2n2
R VR_GT gt gw 1
R VR_GB gw 0 1
R R30 gw ng4 470k
C C26 gw ng4 500p
R R28 ng4 0 470k

* V3A (100k plate load on B+3 with 500p across, 820 / 0.68u cathode) drives V3B, a cathode follower (plate on B+3 through 10k).
T V3A ng4 p4 k4 12AX7
R R27 x2 p4 100k
C C27 x2 p4 500p
R R29 k4 0 820
C C24 k4 0 0.68u
T V3B p4 x3 vb 12AX7
R R31 vb 0 100k
* VOICE (SW3): 470u across V3A's cathode in position 1, 500p on V3B's cathode in position 2.
R SW_V3A k4 c43 1
C C43 c43 0 470u
R SW_V3B vb c42 1e12
C C42 c42 0 500p
* SAT (SW7): 10k + 100n from V3B's cathode into two back-to-back junctions to ground, 1M to ground.
R R33 vb s33 10k
C C25 s33 sat 100n
R SW_SAT sat sat2 1e12
D DZ1 sat2 0 SIGNAL
D DZ2 0 sat2 SIGNAL
R R38 sat2 0 1M

* Tone stack (Marshall arrangement): 500p on the Treble pot (250k), 33k slope, 22n to the Bass (1M, a rheostat) and 22n to the
* Mid pot (25k wiper), then 220k and the Master (1M) with 1M to ground.
C C4 vb tt 500p
R R8 vb m 33k
R VR_TT tt w3 1
R VR_TB w3 n1b 1
C C1 m n1b 22n
R VR_BASS n1b n2b 1
R VR_MIDT n2b wm 1
R VR_MIDB wm 0 1
C C6 m wm 22n
R R59 w3 ms 220k
R R32 ms 0 1M
R VR_MT ms mw 1
R VR_MB mw 0 1

* Clean chain: the tap n1 into 100k and 50p, the passive stack (Treble 1M, Bass 250k, 10k), the Bright caps, the Clean Volume
* (1M), V1B (820 / 10u cathode, 100k plate load), 0.022u and a 470k / 470k divider.
C C10 n1 ct 50p
R R25 n1 cu 100k
C C7 cu cb 0.022u
C C2 cu cbw 0.022u
R VR_CT ct ctw 1
R VR_CB ctw cb 1
R VR_CBT cb cbw2 1
R VR_CBB cbw2 0 1
R R42 cbw2 0 10k
R RCW cbw2 cbw 1
C C11 ctw br1 220p
R SW_BR1 br1 cvw 1
C C12 ctw br2 100p
R SW_BR2 br2 cvw 1e12
R VR_CVT ctw cvw 1
R VR_CVB cvw 0 1
T V1B cvw p5 k5 12AX7
R R12 x p5 100k
R R14 k5 0 820
C C21 k5 0 10u
C C9 p5 cd 0.022u
R R15 cd cl 470k
R R22 cl 0 470k

* RELAY2: the output. Clean sends the clean chain's divider to the power amp, BE and HBE the Master's wiper.
R SW_CLN_OUT cl mo 1
R SW_BE_OUT mw mo 1e12
R RMLOAD mo 0 1M
